/E (These tools are notorious for flagging issues that are not actual problems. Developers can become desensitized to their warnings, leading to "alert fatigue" where even critical alerts are ignored.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 581 0 R
/T (A rule-based system cannot understand the intent behind the code. It might flag a piece of code as a vulnerability when, in that specific context, it is perfectly safe. It doesn't understand the "why," only the "what.")
/E (A rule-based system cannot understand the intent behind the code. It might flag a piece of code as a vulnerability when, in that specific context, it is perfectly safe. It doesn't understand the "why," only the "what.")
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
